WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.773
RUSSIAN SPY ON BRITISH SOIL.

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:05.975
CORRESPONDENT RICH EDSON HAS A

00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:06.475
REACTION TO IT FROM THE

00:00:06.108 --> 00:00:08.310
STATE DEPARTMENT.

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:10.546
&gt;&gt; WE WILL NOT TOLERATE SUCH A

00:00:08.444 --> 00:00:13.816
BRAZEN ATTEMPT TO MURDER

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:14.817
INNOCENT CIVILIANS ON OUR SOIL.

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:16.285
&gt;&gt; BRITISH PRIME MINISTER

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.987
THERESA MAY SAYS IT'S HIGHLY

00:00:16.418 --> 00:00:19.388
LIKELY RUSSIA IS RESPONSIBLE FOR

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.591
POISONING A FORMER SPY WITH

00:00:19.522 --> 00:00:23.792
MILITARY GRADE NERVE AGENT IN

00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:25.995
SOUTHWESTERN ENGLAND.

00:00:23.926 --> 00:00:27.596
HER GOVERNMENT HAS SUMMONED

00:00:26.128 --> 00:00:28.664
RUSSIA'S AMBASSADOR TO THE

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.233
UNITED KINGDOM TO EXPLAIN BY

00:00:28.797 --> 00:00:32.434
TOMORROW WHETHER HIS GOVERNMENT

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.003
EITHER EXECUTED THE ATTACK OR

00:00:32.568 --> 00:00:36.805
LOST CONTROL OF ITS NERVE AGENT.

00:00:34.136 --> 00:00:38.908
&gt;&gt; SHOULD THERE BE NO CREDIBLE

00:00:36.939 --> 00:00:39.808
RESPONSE, WE WILL CONCLUDE THIS

00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:41.510
ACTION AMOUNTS TO AN UNLAWFUL

00:00:39.942 --> 00:00:42.011
USE OF FORCE BY THE RUSSIAN

00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:43.913
STATE AGAINST THE

00:00:42.144 --> 00:00:46.415
UNITED KINGDOM.

00:00:44.046 --> 00:00:48.350
&gt;&gt; MAY AS IT CANNOT BE BUSINESS

00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:49.318
AS USUAL WITH RUSSIA AND BRITAIN

00:00:48.484 --> 00:00:51.153
WOULD CONSIDER MUCH MORE

00:00:49.451 --> 00:00:52.955
EXTENSIVE MEASURES THAN

00:00:51.287 --> 00:00:53.889
DIPLOMATIC EXPULSIONS.

00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:55.991
LAST WEEK, SERGEI SKIPRAL AND

00:00:54.023 --> 00:00:57.026
HIS DAUGHTER WERE FOUND

00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:59.228
POISONED.

00:00:57.159 --> 00:01:01.797
THEY ARE IN THE HOSPITAL IN

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:02.565
CRITICAL STABLE CONDITION.

